# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the CI "thread" leg (run-tests-asan-ubsan.yml).
#
# These are races in the logging and triton core (mempool counters, contexts
# and timers handed between worker threads). They trigger on any log_*() call,
# independent of the l2tp-switch code, and halt_on_error=1 would abort the
# daemon on the first one.
#
# TSAN matches a "race:" entry against EVERY frame of BOTH stacks of a report,
# so "race:foo" hides any race whose stack passes through foo(), however deep.
# Every l2tp callback runs under triton_thread, so a plain "race:triton_thread"
# would hide every race in l2tp.c. "race_top:" matches only the innermost frame
# (the racing access itself), which is what the thread entry needs. A race in
# l2tp.c or l2tp_switch_conf.c is therefore reported unless one of the
# "race:" functions below is on a stack of that report; a report that has one
# is hidden, so keep this list short and do not add broad entries.
# tests/tsan_canary.c checks that the file still lets a race through.
race:mempool_alloc
race:mempool_free
race:unpack_msg
race:general_log
race_top:triton_thread
race:triton_context_unregister
race:triton_queue_ctx
race:md_thread
race:timer_thread
race:triton_timer_del
race:ap_shutdown_soft
# The metrics thread and the "l2tp switch show" command read a target
# tunnel's ->state (an aligned int, stale values are fine there) while the
# tunnel's own context writes it. Only these two tiny functions are listed.
race:l2tp_switch_stat_targets_foreach
race:l2tp_switch_show_exec
